{"id":"chatcmpl-a50af4989d33a9e1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to list the three most serious problems from the codebase. Let me analyze the code carefully.\n\nLet me look at the code for correctness bugs:\n\n1. **`config.ts` - `applyProfile` and `applyActiveProfile` ordering bug**: In `applyRunnerConfig`, the order is:\n```\nsetEnv(ENV.PROFILE, config.profile);\nsetEnv(ENV.MODEL_ID, config.modelId);\n...\napplyCaps(config);\n...\napplyActiveProfile(config);\n```\n\nSo `applyActiveProfile` (which calls `applyProfileByName` → `applyProfile`) runs LAST, which means it overwrites the flat `config.profile`/`config.modelId`/`config.baseUrl`/caps. This is actually the intended behavior (profile wins over flat). But wait — there's a subtle issue: `applyProfile` sets `ENV.PROFILE` to `baseProfileFor(profile.backend)` (e.g., `","signature":"07e2f10ecf39455484fb54bb46e88be4"}],"model":"qwen38-27b-mxfp4-dflash","stop_reason":"max_tokens","usage":{"input_tokens":1098,"output_tokens":200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5280,"cache_read_input_tokens":27280}}